title: Basil Bramwell
from: Basil Bramwell
gist: Basil heard about the transfer. You can't go, he said: you're his mentor. Then he took it back, mostly.
== lines
bramwell-basil: You can't go. You're my mentor. Is that a rule? It should be a rule. Is it a rule?   [gesture]
bramwell-basil: Sorry. That came out all at once. Halloran told me. Is it true? Are you? Are you sure?
bramwell-basil > you: I've only just learnt where the tea is. And which coil sulks. You taught me that.
? choice
* You'd be fine without me.   flavour:cheer
  bramwell-basil: Would I? I would. Probably. The plant wouldn't. Don't tell it.   [laugh]
* I haven't decided yet.   flavour:listen
  bramwell-basil: Oh. Good. Not good. Fair. Brilliant. Take ages. Take until Sunday.
bramwell-basil: In the Ostrander colonies we'd throw you a party either way. We'll do it here. Bigger.
